\f0\fs24 \cf0 Organization Policies\
Make sure your organization (riosinstitute.org) is selected in the top project picker.\
\
Go to the main menu (\uc0\u9776 ).\
\
Select IAM & Admin.\
\
Select Organization Policies.\
\
2. Find and Edit the Policy\
In the Filter box, type: vmExternalIpAccess\
\
Click on the policy name: "External IPs for VM instances".\
\
Click the Edit Policy button at the top of the details page.\
\
3. Change the Policy for vecinita\
On the "Edit policy" screen, select Customize.\
\
Click Add rule.\
\
On the new rule card:\
\
Enforcement: Select Allow.\
\
Now, tell it to apply this "Allow" rule only to your project:\
\
Click Add resource.\
\
A panel will open on the right.\
\
Resource type: Select Project.\
\
Resource ID: Type your Project ID: vecinita\
\
Click Done.\
\
Click Save.\
\
That's it for the first one. You've now given your vecinita project permission to use external IPs. You can test this by going to your VM and trying to add one\'97the option should now be available.\
\
